# Read-only snapshots of the instance. Regenerate with tools/dump_states.py.
# Not committed: they are large, they churn, and they contain the full entity
# list of a private home.
tools/states.json
tools/registry.json
tools/preview_states.js
.DS_Store
tools/house_roles.json
# Same map as house_roles.json, in the form the preview harness loads it.
tools/preview_roles.js

# --- instance data: never publish -------------------------------------------
# This repo is public. Everything below describes THIS house -- which rooms
# exist, who sleeps in them, what watches the doors -- and none of it is needed
# to install or read the cards.
#
# The generated dashboard, with the whole role map injected into it.
tools/house_dash.json
# Dashboard backups taken before each deploy. Same content, one per deploy.
tools/backup_the-house_*.json
# What was last deployed or pulled, so deploy_dash.py can tell a hand edit made
# in HA from its own last write. Same private content as the dashboard itself.
tools/.deployed_*.json
# The map itself: people, rooms, devices. gen_roles.py holds the logic and
# imports the facts from here, so the published repo describes the machinery
# without describing the household.
tools/house_private.py
